{
 "source": "lanes/per-type-facts/approved-byte-differences.md, entries 1 to 15 as of 11-27 18:05Z (entry 15 judges mock worlds by compiling and executed trace; entry 14 is covered by entry 2's comparison). Matching an entry classifies a difference; each entry's conditions (compile, executed values) still gate it.",
 "entries": [
  {
   "id": "9-keyword-member-in-backticks",
   "ruling": "lead 11-27 9:31 AM PT",
   "summary": "An override member named like a keyword goes in backticks.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "line": "(safeDIOverrides(?:\\.(?:\\w+|`[^`]+`))*)\\.`(\\w+)`",
     "replacement": "\\1.\\2",
     "side": "head",
     "repeat": true
    }
   ],
   "scope": "mock"
  },
  {
   "id": "3-configuration-local-goes",
   "ruling": "11-27, for mockActor",
   "summary": "The local that held a function's configuration goes where the function is handed it.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "dropLine": "^let __safeDI_\\w+__overrides = ",
     "side": "base"
    },
    {
     "line": "\\b__safeDI_\\w+__overrides\\b",
     "replacement": "safeDIOverrides",
     "side": "base"
    }
   ],
   "scope": "mock"
  },
  {
   "id": "5-unavailable-override-argument",
   "status": "withdrawn",
   "ruling": "withdrawn by the lead 11-27 17:35Z: the override is an ordinary read from above bound by mock()",
   "summary": "The old form: an override of an unavailable dependency handed down as further arguments after safeDIOverrides:.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "line": "^((?:@\\w+ )*(?:nonisolated )?func (?:__safeDI_\\w+|`__safeDI_[^`]+`)\\(.*?safeDIOverrides: (?:[^(),<>]|<[^<>]*>|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:[^()])*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\))+?)(?:, \\w+: (?:[^(),<>]|<[^<>]*>|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:[^()])*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\))+?)+(?=\\) (?:async |throws )*-> )",
     "replacement": "\\1",
     "side": "head"
    },
    {
     "line": "((?:__safeDI_\\w+|`__safeDI_[^`]+`)\\((?:[^()]*?, )?)(\\w+): safeDIOverrides\\.\\2(?:, |(?=\\)))",
     "replacement": "\\1",
     "side": "head",
     "repeat": true
    }
   ],
   "shapes": [
    "changed: ? = {- safeDIOverrides . -} X1"
   ],
   "scope": "mock"
  },
  {
   "id": "1-overrides-handed-as-argument",
   "ruling": "lead's mock world ruling; entry 15 (11-27 17:52Z) judges it by compiling and executed trace",
   "summary": "A function is handed its node's overrides as an argument and reads them where the walk spelled the whole path.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "line": "^((?:@\\w+ )*(?:nonisolated )?func (?:__safeDI_\\w+|`__safeDI_[^`]+`)\\(.*?)(?:, )?safeDIOverrides: (?:[^(),<>]|<[^<>]*>|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:[^()])*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\))+?(?=\\) (?:async |throws )*-> )",
     "replacement": "\\1"
    },
    {
     "line": "(?:, )?safeDIOverrides: safeDIOverrides(?:\\.(?:\\w+|`[^`]+`))*",
     "replacement": ""
    },
    {
     "line": "(?:, )?safeDIOverrides: __safeDI_\\w+__safeDIBuilder\\b",
     "replacement": ""
    },
    {
     "line": "if let safeDIBuilder = __safeDI_\\w+__safeDIBuilder \\{",
     "replacement": "if let safeDIBuilder = safeDIOverrides {"
    },
    {
     "line": "\\(, ",
     "replacement": "("
    },
    {
     "line": "safeDIOverrides(?:\\.(?:\\w+|`[^`]+`))*(\\.(?:\\w+|`[^`]+`))",
     "replacement": "safeDIOverrides\\1"
    },
    {
     "line": "if let safeDIBuilder = safeDIOverrides\\.(?!safeDIBuilder\\b)(?:\\w+|`[^`]+`) \\{",
     "replacement": "if let safeDIBuilder = safeDIOverrides {"
    }
   ],
   "scope": "mock"
  },
  {
   "id": "2-one-function-per-node",
   "ruling": "lead's mock world ruling; entry 15",
   "summary": "One function per node, declared once in the root's body and called by each parent; a function moved there takes the values it captured as parameters, and a wrapper that calls it with arguments is a closure. A head function equal to one of the base's bodies of its name is accepted, which also covers entry 14 (one @Sendable function for a Sendable lazy twin and a constant twin).",
   "steps": [
    {
     "hoistFunctions": "^(?:@Sendable )?(?:nonisolated )?func (?P<name>(?:__safeDI_\\w+|`__safeDI_[^`]+`))\\("
    },
    {
     "line": "^((?:@\\w+ )*(?:nonisolated )?func (?:__safeDI_\\w+|`__safeDI_[^`]+`)\\()(?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:[^()])*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*?(?=\\) (?:async |throws )*-> )",
     "replacement": "\\1"
    },
    {
     "line": "((?:__safeDI_\\w+|`__safeDI_[^`]+`)\\((?:[^()]*?, )?)(\\w+|`[^`]+`): \\2(?:, |(?=\\)))",
     "replacement": "\\1",
     "repeat": true
    },
    {
     "line": ", \\)",
     "replacement": ")",
     "repeat": true
    },
    {
     "text": "((?:Sendable)?(?:Erased)?(?:Instantiator|LazilyInstantiated)<[^\\n]*>) \\{\\n\\s*((?:try |await )*)((?:__safeDI_\\w+|`__safeDI_[^`]+`))\\(\\)\\n\\s*\\}",
     "replacement": "\\1(\\3)"
    }
   ],
   "shapes": [
    "changed: > ( {- __safeDI_X1 -}{+ __safeDI_X2 +} )",
    "function removed: func __safeDI_X1 ( ) -> X2 {"
   ],
   "scope": "mock"
  },
  {
   "id": "4-wrapper-binding-spells-type",
   "ruling": "11-27, erased, sendable and default-valued parameter kinds",
   "summary": "A wrapper binding of a type declared in an extension spells its type, as production's does.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "line": "^let (\\w+): ((?:Sendable)?(?:Erased)?Instantiator<.*>) = \\2(?=[({ ]|$)",
     "replacement": "let \\1 = \\2",
     "side": "head"
    }
   ],
   "scope": "mock"
  },
  {
   "id": "7-alias-chain-roots-flat",
   "scope": "production",
   "ruling": "lead 11-27 12:54Z and 15:38Z, for exactly these nine roots",
   "summary": "A root with a label-keeping rename of a rename is laid out by the type key: builder functions declared once in the root's body, a function that reads the outer rename takes it as a parameter.",
   "conditions": "Executed values equal 2.4.1's in each case; no root without a rename of a rename moves.",
   "tests": [
    "generate_bindsChainToNil_whenReaderBeneathLabelKeepingAliasOfAliasOfPropertyBeingBuiltReceivesIt",
    "generate_bindsErasedLabelKeepingAliasFromAlias_whenItRetypesAliasAboveIt",
    "generate_bindsLabelKeepingAliasFromAliasAbove_whenItSpellsUnwrappedFormBeneathAlias",
    "generate_bindsLabelKeepingAliasFromAliasInSeamsModule_whenItAndItsDeclaringTypeAreInModuleSeamDependsOn",
    "generate_bindsLabelKeepingAliasFromAlias_whenItRetypesAliasAboveIt",
    "generate_bindsLabelKeepingAliasFromAlias_whenReaderBeneathLabelKeepingAliasOfAliasReceivesIt",
    "generate_bindsLabelKeepingAliasFromNearestDeclaration_whenItIsReachedBeneathAliasAndBesideIt",
    "run_passesNilToOnlyIfAvailableReceiverOfSiblingRequiringTheReceiversAncestor_whenAncestorsTreeAlsoAliasesSiblingsOptionalFormBeneathForwardedSibling",
    "run_passesNilToOnlyIfAvailableReceiverOfEarlierSiblingRequiringTheReceiversAncestor_whenAncestorsTreeAlsoAliasesSiblingsOptionalFormBeneathForwardedSibling"
   ],
   "steps": [
    {
     "hoistFunctions": "^(?:@Sendable )?(?:nonisolated )?func (?P<name>(?:__safeDI_\\w+|`__safeDI_[^`]+`))\\("
    },
    {
     "line": "^((?:@\\w+ )*(?:nonisolated )?func (?:__safeDI_\\w+|`__safeDI_[^`]+`)\\()(?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:(?:[^()]|\\((?:[^()])*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*\\)))*?(?=\\) (?:async |throws )*-> )",
     "replacement": "\\1"
    },
    {
     "line": "((?:__safeDI_\\w+|`__safeDI_[^`]+`)\\((?:[^()]*?, )?)(\\w+|`[^`]+`): \\2(?:, |(?=\\)))",
     "replacement": "\\1",
     "repeat": true
    },
    {
     "line": ", \\)",
     "replacement": ")",
     "repeat": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "6-unlabeled-argument-spelled",
   "ruling": "lead's test, 11-27",
   "summary": "An argument of a parameter with no label is spelled `_: value`, as production spells it.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "line": "([(,] ?)_: ",
     "replacement": "\\1",
     "side": "head"
    }
   ],
   "scope": "mock"
  },
  {
   "id": "8-constant-binding-states-type",
   "ruling": "lead 11-27 9:31 AM PT",
